{%- comment -%}
  Besjaar 11.6.8 — cart drawer.

  1. The payment-logo row is dropped so the line items and the checkout
     button get the space. Everything else in the drawer is the theme's
     original design.
  2. Resilience for cart updates ("Winkelwagen kon niet worden bijgewerkt"):
     - cart writes (/cart/change.js, /cart/update.js, /cart/add.js,
       /cart/clear.js) run one at a time, so a burst of +/− taps can no
       longer overlap;
     - a quantity update or cart read that fails on the network or with a
       5xx is retried once after 450 ms before the theme shows its error.
       add.js is never retried (a lost response could otherwise add twice);
       4xx answers (e.g. stock limits) are passed through untouched.
     This wraps window.fetch after the runtime section's wrapper, so the
     one-round-trip optimisation there keeps working.

  Temporary carrier; fold into assets/besjaar-ui-core.js during consolidation.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  2026-11-05 performance: besjaar-x-cart-1.css and besjaar-cart-ux.css style only
  the cart drawer and the cart page (every rule is scoped to #BesjaarUICartDrawer,
  the drawer classes or body[data-page-type="cart"]). The closed drawer is already
  off-screen and inert from besjaar-seo-base.css in <head>, so outside the cart page
  these two files load without blocking the first paint (media="print" swap). The
  <link> keeps its place in the document, so the cascade order is unchanged once
  they apply. On the cart page they stay render-blocking as before.
  Not done for besjaar-x-cart-mobile-1.css: it hides the express-checkout buttons
  ([data-bj-cd-express]) until they are moved into the drawer.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'cart' -%}
  {{ 'besjaar-x-cart-1.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}
{%- else -%}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'besjaar-x-cart-1.css' | asset_url }}" media="print" onload="this.media='all'">
  <noscript>{{ 'besjaar-x-cart-1.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}</noscript>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}2026-11-05 performance: assets/besjaar-x-cart-2.js (the fetch queue) now loads from layout/theme.liquid (<head>, defer, before besjaar-ui-core.js); besjaar-x-cart-3.js is deferred. Both were parser-blocking here.{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'besjaar-x-cart-3.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- comment -%}
  2026-09-29: one gold (#E0A526) for every review star on every page –
  collection and search cards, product page, homepage, cart. Older theme rules
  painted stars navy, amber (#D79545) or a darker gold, some with an id in the
  selector. The two :not(#…) parts only raise specificity (no element has
  those ids), so this rule wins over any of them.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'besjaar-x-cart-4.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}
{%- comment -%}
  2026-11-05 cart drawer UX: the drawer shows the same short product names as
  the cart page (handle -> name from snippets/localized-product-title.liquid,
  applied by assets/besjaar-cart-ux.js) and the free-shipping band is visible
  again, with compact suggestion cards (assets/besjaar-cart-ux.css).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture bj_cart_titles -%}
  {%- for bj_tp in collections['all'].products limit: 50 -%}
    {%- capture bj_tt -%}{% render 'localized-product-title', product: bj_tp %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- unless forloop.first -%},{%- endunless -%}{{ bj_tp.handle | json }}:{{ bj_tt | strip | json }}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
<script type="application/json" data-bj-cart-titles>{ {{- bj_cart_titles -}} }</script>
{%- if request.page_type == 'cart' -%}
  {{ 'besjaar-cart-ux.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}
{%- else -%}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'besjaar-cart-ux.css' | asset_url }}" media="print" onload="this.media='all'">
  <noscript>{{ 'besjaar-cart-ux.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}</noscript>
{%- endif -%}
<script src="{{ 'besjaar-cart-ux.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- comment -%}
  2026-11-05 product page UX (assets/besjaar-product-ux.css, product pages only):
  the add-to-cart button comes straight after the price and version choice (the
  Club member-price box moves below the delivery line) and on desktop all
  product photos fit on one thumbnail row.
  2026-11-05 collection page UX (assets/besjaar-collection-ux.css, collection
  pages only): a lower title band, three cards per row from 761px and four from
  1100px, and a plus on the quick-add button.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}{{ 'besjaar-product-ux.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}{%- endif -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'collection' -%}{{ 'besjaar-collection-ux.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}{%- endif -%}
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Besjaar cart polish",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "11.6.8 + 2026-09-30 (Univex cart: 440px, with a 300px suggestions column from 1100px): hides the payment-logo row in the cart drawer, queues cart updates so quick taps cannot overlap, and retries a failed quantity update once before the theme shows its error. Keep in the header group after the runtime section."
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
